🚀 HR Management System – Backend API

A scalable, secure, and real-time HR Management System Backend API built using ASP.NET Core Web API.
This project is designed to simulate a real-world enterprise HR system with modular architecture, role-based access, and real-time communication features.

📌 Overview

This system goes beyond basic CRUD operations and focuses on real-world backend architecture, including:

Multi-tenant organization-based structure
Role-based access control (Admin, HR, Employee)
Real-time communication system
Scalable backend design principles
🏗️ Architecture

The project follows a Clean Layered Architecture:

Controllers → Services → Repositories → Database
Key Design Principles:
Separation of concerns
Scalable modular structure
Maintainable service-based logic
Secure authentication flow
⚙️ Tech Stack
.NET 6 / ASP.NET Core Web API
Entity Framework Core
SQL Server
JWT Authentication
SignalR (Real-time Communication)
Redis (Caching, Presence, Scalability)
Dependency Injection
LINQ
🔐 Authentication & Authorization
JWT-based authentication
Role-based authorization:
Admin
HR
Employee
Secure API endpoints with policy-based access control
Organization-level multi-tenant isolation
💬 Real-Time Chat System

A major highlight of this project is the real-time chat module:

Features:
Built using SignalR
Instant messaging between:
Employee ↔ HR
Employee ↔ Admin
Strict access control (no employee-to-employee chat)
Real-time message delivery without page refresh
Scalability Enhancements:
Redis integration
User presence tracking
Distributed caching
Improved performance under load
Designed for multi-instance backend deployment
